c1. Minimal phi^6 coefficient: V = lam_eff(h) h^4/4 + c h^6/M^2 >= V_EW (~ -1.2e8 GeV^4, negligible) for all h <= M_P
   M = 1/a = M_P    c_min = 4.373e+11 at h = 2.916e+11 GeV (instability scale h_I = 1.81e+11); equivalent unit-coefficient scale Lambda_6 = M/sqrt(c_min) = 1.846e+13 GeV
   M = reduced M_P  c_min = 1.739e+10 at h = 2.916e+11 GeV (instability scale h_I = 1.81e+11); equivalent unit-coefficient scale Lambda_6 = M/sqrt(c_min) = 1.846e+13 GeV

c2. With an O(1) Planck-suppressed coefficient the potential is bounded below but a deeper minimum remains:
   c =    0.1 : V_min = -9.943e+69 GeV^4 at h = 1.747e+18 GeV (h a = 0.143) ; Lambda_tilde/rho_Lambda = kappa(V_EW - E0)/rho_L = 3.98e+116
   c =    1.0 : V_min = -1.009e+68 GeV^4 at h = 5.596e+17 GeV (h a = 0.046) ; Lambda_tilde/rho_Lambda = kappa(V_EW - E0)/rho_L = 4.04e+114
   c =   10.0 : V_min = -1.001e+66 GeV^4 at h = 1.769e+17 GeV (h a = 0.014) ; Lambda_tilde/rho_Lambda = kappa(V_EW - E0)/rho_L = 4.00e+112
   c =  100.0 : V_min = -9.685e+63 GeV^4 at h = 5.519e+16 GeV (h a = 0.005) ; Lambda_tilde/rho_Lambda = kappa(V_EW - E0)/rho_L = 3.87e+110
   (h a ~ O(0.1-1) means this minimum sits where the EFT itself is at the lattice scale: a reading, not a computation)

c3. The lattice's own dispersion: dimension-6 coefficient generated by the one-loop zero-point sum of a field
    with field-dependent mass M = y h/sqrt2, lattice minus continuum, Delta V ~ c_lat h^6 a^2 (a = 1/M_P).
   box law (exact relativistic inside the cube): Ma = 1e-01 : I = -1.79907e-03
   box law (exact relativistic inside the cube): Ma = 3e-02 : I = -1.79728e-03
   box law (exact relativistic inside the cube): Ma = 1e-02 : I = -1.79902e-03
   box law, M -> 0: J = -I = 1.79893e-03  (bound: outside inscribed sphere gives 1/(4 pi^4) = 2.56650e-03)
   nearest-neighbour (sin) boson: Ma = 0.30 : I = +1.2732e-02  (IR-log grows like ln(1/Ma) as Ma -> 0: a^2 M^6 ln term)
   nearest-neighbour (sin) boson: Ma = 0.10 : I = +2.0022e-02  (IR-log grows like ln(1/Ma) as Ma -> 0: a^2 M^6 ln term)
   nearest-neighbour (sin) boson: Ma = 0.05 : I = +2.4437e-02  (IR-log grows like ln(1/Ma) as Ma -> 0: a^2 M^6 ln term)
   top (n = 12, y_t(1e11) = 0.510), box law: c_lat = (1/6)(n/2)(3/8) J (y^2/2)^3 = +1.49e-06 (stabilizing sign)
   sin-law, log-extrapolated to the physical Ma = y h_I a/sqrt2 = 5.32e-09: |I| ~ 1.28e-01 -> |c_lat| ~ 1.06e-04
   compare c_min(M = 1/a) from c1: lattice dimension-6 terms fall short by a factor >= 4.1e+15

c4. Field-range reading: if the qubit-composite Higgs amplitude were bounded by h_max, stability needs h_max < h_I:
   h_I = 1.81e+11 GeV -> h_max a < 1.5e-08 (a stipulated small number, not a lattice-scale O(1) term)
